WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.840
Hi, Mystery Recapped here.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:09.940
Today I am going to explain an American dystopian
drama film called “Fahrenheit 451.”

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.160
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:17.200
Watch out and take care!

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.840
The movie is set in a futuristic dystopian
world.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:26.710
After the second civil war, an absolute dictatorship
of the “Ministry” took over the United

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:27.710
States.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:32.910
Under the dictatorship, people called “Firemen”
are appointed to burn every single existing

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:38.030
book so people won’t get the knowledge that
the Ministry doesn’t want them to know.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:43.380
The books are replaced by the Internet, called
"the 9" which consists of very limited reading

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.790
materials allowed by the ministry.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:50.620
In the opening scene, we are introduced to
a fireman named Guy Montag.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:55.040
He is in his futuristic house talking to an
AI that helps him dress up.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:00.280
Montag has always been taught that reading
books is a crime that will cause unhappiness,

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:02.900
mental illness, and conflicting opinions.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:07.850
He has never questioned the principles of
the Ministry and works hard as a fireman.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:12.890
While getting ready, Montag listens to the
news about book reading and preserving maniacs

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:14.420
called the Eels.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:18.990
Eels are considered criminals by law just
for trying to preserve books and the knowledge

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:19.990
in them.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:24.880
Montag goes to work that morning to teach
the kids about the principles of the Ministry.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:29.640
He and his mentor Captain John Beatty tell
the kids that the only books they should read

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:35.380
are the books assigned by the ministry, namely;
The Bible, To the Lighthouse, and Moby Dick.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:40.130
Montag also burns two books for a demonstration
as the crowd cheers for him.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:43.479
At night, they are alerted of Eels on the
move.

00:01:43.479 --> 00:01:48.299
Beatty, Montag, and their crew of firemen
quickly drive to the location while singing

00:01:48.299 --> 00:01:49.869
songs about their bravery.

00:01:49.869 --> 00:01:54.280
They reach a house where a couple is trying
to upload books on the internet for everyone

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.280
to read.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.110
The firemen quickly stop them and break their
computers.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:02.450
Montag then takes them outside and insults
them in front of the reporters.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:10.829
He also burns a pile of books in front of
the camera as the people watching cheer for

00:02:10.829 --> 00:02:13.930
him.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:17.069
While burning them, Montag gets flashes of
his late father.

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:18.310
He seizes the man’s citizenship and declares
him an Eel by law.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:23.290
Later, Beatty and Montag go to a club and
meet a girl named Clarisse McClellan.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:27.290
Clarisse was once declared an Eel and has
been on a restriction since then.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:32.909
She asks Beatty to take a year off her restriction
in turn for reporting other Eels in the town,

00:02:32.909 --> 00:02:34.209
and he agrees.

00:02:34.209 --> 00:02:39.260
He and Montag go to the address she provides
and find an old man shooting a video.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:43.189
The man is a civil war survivor who tells
them that firemen are supposed to put out

00:02:43.189 --> 00:02:45.230
fires, not create them.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:48.780
Beatty doesn’t believe him claiming it to
be a classic Eel lie.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:54.370
However, the old man’s words strike Montag
and he begins to question if it is the truth.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.620
The firemen have been told that the creator
of the fire department, Benjamin Franklin

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.730
has given them the right to burn.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:05.409
But the man laughs at them for believing such
absurd lies fed by the ministry.

00:03:05.409 --> 00:03:09.169
He is soon arrested and people praise firemen
for their bravery.

00:03:09.169 --> 00:03:12.589
Before going home, Montag and Beatty go to
a bar to drink.

00:03:12.589 --> 00:03:17.549
Montag talks about his father being a great
fireman who died while in service.

00:03:17.549 --> 00:03:22.060
We find out that after his father’s death,
Montag was raised by Beatty who treats him

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.420
like a brother.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:28.739
Later at night, Clarisse meets an informer
and exchanges a music recorder for information.

00:03:28.739 --> 00:03:33.030
The man tells her about a house in the woods
that is a drop-off spot for books.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:38.189
When Montag reaches home, he asks the AI if
firemen used to put out fires before the civil

00:03:38.189 --> 00:03:39.189
war.

00:03:39.189 --> 00:03:43.459
The AI declares it a lie and asks Montag if
his vitals are fluctuating.

00:03:43.459 --> 00:03:48.120
It also suggests he take a mandatory prescribed
medicine called drops.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.699
Montag soon gets a call from Beatty and the
two go to the house in the woods that Clarisse

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:54.669
has informed them about.

00:03:54.669 --> 00:03:57.419
Inside the house is an old woman reading a
book.

00:03:57.419 --> 00:04:01.119
She doesn’t react to the firemen breaking
in and continues reading.

00:04:01.119 --> 00:04:03.949
They snatch the book from her to get her attention.

00:04:03.949 --> 00:04:10.089
Just then, a fireman calls everyone upstairs
to a library containing hundreds of books.

00:04:10.089 --> 00:04:13.790
Montag is stunned as he has never seen so
many books at once.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:18.269
Beatty asks him to take in the scene before
him because he might never see something like

00:04:18.269 --> 00:04:19.359
this again.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:23.639
He also hands one of the books to the guy
and asks him to read the first line.

00:04:23.639 --> 00:04:26.900
Montag nervously reads it but is stopped midway.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:32.120
Beatty concludes it as an example of how quickly
their minds can be diverted by books.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:36.630
After Beatty leaves the room, curiosity gets
the best of Montag and he secretly hides a

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.479
book under his shirt.

00:04:38.479 --> 00:04:43.090
After that, the firemen gather all the books
downstairs and pour gasoline on them.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:48.480
The old woman sits quietly the whole time
but when she is asked to move outside, she

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:49.480
refuses.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:55.409
Instead, the lady walks in the middle of the
pile of books and burns herself with them.

00:04:55.409 --> 00:04:58.810
Before dying he says a single word; Omnis.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:03.430
Montag watches in horror as the scent of burning
flesh fills the room.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:08.520
Along with him, the rest of the world also
watches the lady burn through live television.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:13.210
After the commotion, Beatty is called by his
senior who accuses him of being careless.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:17.729
He states that the word “Omnis” has taken
over the internet so, in the revised video

00:05:17.729 --> 00:05:21.050
of the woman, he wants her to say “Coward”.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:25.870
The following day, Montag notices the change
in the video and confronts Beatty about it.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:31.180
He wants to know what the word Omnis means
and Beatty reveals that it means “everything”.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:35.880
He uses the woman’s suicide as an example
to prove that reading books affects mental

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:36.880
health.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:41.819
When Montag reaches home at night, he asks
his AI to turn off and reads the book he had

00:05:41.819 --> 00:05:42.819
hidden.

00:05:42.819 --> 00:05:46.600
While reading out loud, the AI corrects him
in one of the lines.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:51.680
A surprised Montag asks why it didn’t turn
off when the AI replies that the conversation

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.760
is just between the two of them.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:57.949
Montag doesn’t feel safe in his own home,
so he runs out quickly.

00:05:57.949 --> 00:06:00.939
He eventually ends up in the area near Clarisse’s
house.

00:06:00.939 --> 00:06:06.250
She first threatens him to stay away but agrees
to talk to him after seeing the book.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:09.720
The two go to Clarisse’s apartment and read
the book together.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.590
She also informs him that the ministry has
been turning people illiterate so they can

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:15.070
rule over them.

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:19.780
After the civil war, they have been slowly
killing people taking over cultures to create

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.860
a single absolute rule.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:26.560
She then reveals that the drops Montag takes
every day are to wipe his childhood memories

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:30.039
and to make him docile so he wouldn't question
the system.

00:06:30.039 --> 00:06:33.490
Clarisse was born to Eel parents and was an
Eel herself.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:38.830
But as she grew up, she got tired of living
life on a run so she came to the city disguised

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.139
as a native.

00:06:40.139 --> 00:06:44.900
However, she soon got bored and started smuggling
books again, only to be caught.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:47.460
Hence, currently, she is in restriction.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:50.129
The night ends as the two play harmonica together.

00:06:50.129 --> 00:06:53.949
When Montag returns home, he is an entirely
different person.

00:06:53.949 --> 00:06:58.500
He doesn’t take the drops that day, to test
if Clarisse is really telling the truth.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:02.889
Because of this, he gets a flashback of the
time when he was little and his father used

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:04.190
to give him books.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:08.659
Beatty holds a meeting the next day and reveals
that some Eels have been able to code the

00:07:08.659 --> 00:07:12.260
knowledge of thousands of books into DNA.

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:16.879
That code is called the Omnis and the Eels
are planning to send the Omnis to Canada to

00:07:16.879 --> 00:07:17.999
be distributed.

00:07:17.999 --> 00:07:22.750
If that happens, the world will have access
to all the books ever written and the entire

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.219
purpose of the firemen will be insignificant.

00:07:25.219 --> 00:07:30.110
To quickly find the Omnis, all the firemen
come together and collect Eels hiding throughout

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:31.879
the city in a warehouse.

00:07:31.879 --> 00:07:36.629
They hit and torture the poor men for the
information but they do not budge.

00:07:36.629 --> 00:07:39.520
Clarisse is also caught by the firemen and
brought there.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:43.960
Montag quietly stays behind Beatty and observes
the people being beaten.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:48.810
He catches one of the Eels trying to run away
and again get flashbacks of his past.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:53.539
This time, he sees some firemen hitting his
father with a pile of books on the ground.

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:57.669
Back in teh present, all the Eels are kept
in a line and threatened but none of them

00:07:57.669 --> 00:07:59.580
reveal where the Omnis is.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:04.289
Suddenly, Montag switches the lights off giving
the Eels a chance to run away.

00:08:04.289 --> 00:08:09.789
The firemen run around to catch them but Clarisse
manages to escape along with a few other Eels.

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:13.529
While pretending to look for them, Montag
finds a little girl and her father hiding

00:08:13.529 --> 00:08:14.639
in a bathroom.

00:08:14.639 --> 00:08:17.620
He simply closes the shower curtains and leaves.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:21.009
However, Beatty sees him doing this and arrests
the Eels.

00:08:21.009 --> 00:08:26.039
Later, Beatty calls Montag in his office and
furiously asks him why he pretended like he

00:08:26.039 --> 00:08:27.289
didn’t see the criminals.

00:08:27.289 --> 00:08:31.639
Montag says it is because of the little girl,
he felt compassionate towards the Eels, to

00:08:31.639 --> 00:08:36.909
which Beatty replies that they often use kids
as decoys, so Montag should be tougher.

00:08:36.909 --> 00:08:41.839
Montag then takes his jacket off and hands
it to Beatty, resigning from his position.

00:08:41.839 --> 00:08:46.210
An enraged Beatty throws the jacket at him
claiming that he didn’t spend so much time

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:50.140
teaching him the Ministry’s principle for
him to resign that easily.

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:54.660
He threatens to burn Montag to ashes if he
ever betrays him.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:59.180
After the interaction, Beatty assigns another
officer to keep an eye on Montag.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:04.370
A while later, we see Montag and Clarisse
meet Clarisse is with her fellow Eel friends

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:07.889
who ask Montag to get in the car and drive
away.

00:09:07.889 --> 00:09:12.019
It is evident that the Eels are not fond of
him but Clarisse assures them he is on their

00:09:12.019 --> 00:09:13.019
side.

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:17.949
Meanwhile, Beatty sees a video of Montag getting
inside an Eel’s car and is furious at the

00:09:17.949 --> 00:09:18.949
betrayal.

00:09:18.949 --> 00:09:23.610
Montag is blindfolded and taken to a secret
Eel hideout where he meets Clarisse’s friends

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:24.810
and mentors.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:30.060
All of them have memorized one book each so
even if they are found, the books exist forever.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:34.220
To test Montag’s loyalty, they ask him to
kill a fireman they have captured.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:39.540
Montag is about to stab the guy but the others
stop him, telling him that he has passed.

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:44.250
After finally being accepted into the team,
he is told about a young guy named Clifford.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:49.550
He possesses a bird that has the DNA encoded
with the books, called the Omnis.

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:54.690
Clifford’s mother was the geneticist who
created Omnis and injected it into the bird.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:10:00.410
Now, the Canadian scientists have taken responsibility
to duplicate the bird’s DNA and inject it

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:05.009
into every other animal in the world, so the
information inside the books can spread.

00:10:05.009 --> 00:10:09.970
Hence, they need Montag’s help to send the
bird to a group of scientists in Canada.

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:16.060
Montag then meets Clifford who is a genius
with over 1300 books memorized.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:21.019
Montag picks up a random book from Clifford’s
collection to test him and is pleasantly surprised

00:10:21.019 --> 00:10:22.589
by his unique skill.

00:10:22.589 --> 00:10:26.959
He is tasked to bring a transponder from the
fire department because the Canadian scientists

00:10:26.959 --> 00:10:29.709
are transmitting a homing signal to find the
bird.

00:10:29.709 --> 00:10:34.110
Unknown that Beatty knows his secret, Montag
goes to the fire department.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:38.200
He walks inside the building with ease and
manages to get a transponder.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.480
But before he can leave, he encounters Beatty.

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.829
Beatty asks him if he still wants to resign.

00:10:43.829 --> 00:10:47.389
Montag plays along and says he is ready for
a raid.

00:10:47.389 --> 00:10:50.120
The two gear up and drive to the supposed
raid.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:54.220
But they stop in front of Montag’s home
where the media has gathered to report shocking

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:55.850
information about him.

00:10:55.850 --> 00:11:00.550
Montag doesn't question anyone and simply
walks inside to find a pile of books on the

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:01.550
floor.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:05.680
The firemen claim that the books were found
in his house and falsely accuse him of being

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:06.680
an Eel.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:10.790
Beatty asks him to burn the books on the floor
and he obliges.

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:15.510
Just then, he gets a flashback of Beatty arresting
his father for owning books.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.970
But unfortunately, he cannot do anything.

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:20.420
He is brought outside and declared an Eel.

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:24.800
Suddenly, Montag gets his hands on a gun and
manages to flee.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:28.550
Clarisse picks him up in her car and the two
drive to the secret hideout.

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:32.440
However, before they get there, the place
is raided by the firemen.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:37.459
They set fire to all the books and kill most
of Clarisse’s friends and mentors.

00:11:37.459 --> 00:11:42.220
When Montag reaches there, he sneaks into
the burning barn and finds Clifford’s dead

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:43.220
body.

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:46.040
Thankfully, the bird is still alive inside
a cage.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:51.610
As he ties a transponder to its feet, Beatty
appears behind him and asks him to stop.

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:55.570
Montag looks him dead in the eyes and sets
the bird free.

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:59.920
After it flies away, an enraged Beatty burns
Montag alive.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:05.060
In the last scene, we see the bird joining
with an immense flock over Canada.

